.TH FQDNMGR 1 "2026-07-06" "a2tools 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
fqdnmgr \- provision domains: ownership checks, purchases and DNS records
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fqdnmgr
.RB [ \-\-help "] [" \-v | \-\-verbose ]
.B fqdnmgr check
.RB [ \-d " " \fIFQDN\fR]
.RB [ \-r " " \fIREGISTRAR\fR]
.B fqdnmgr purchase
.RB [ \-d " " \fIFQDN\fR]
.RB [ \-r " " \fIREGISTRAR\fR]
.B fqdnmgr certify
.RB [ \-r " " \fIREGISTRAR\fR]
.B fqdnmgr cleanup
.RB [ \-r " " \fIREGISTRAR\fR]
.B fqdnmgr setInitDNSRecords
.RB [ \-d " " \fIFQDN\fR]
.RB [ \-r " " \fIREGISTRAR\fR]
.RB [ \-o | \-\-override ]
.RB [ \-\-sync ]
.RB [ \-\-timeout " " \fISECONDS\fR]
.B fqdnmgr checkInitDns
.RB [ \-d " " \fIFQDN\fR]
.B fqdnmgr list
.RB [ \-r " " \fIREGISTRAR\fR]
.RB [ \-m " " { \fBlocal\fR | \fBremote\fR } ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBfqdnmgr\fR interacts with domain registrars (Namecheap, Wedos, ...)
through a small plugin interface to check domain availability, purchase
domains, list domains on an account, and set DNS records. It also
implements the auth / cleanup hooks used by \fBcertbot\fR for ACME
DNS\-01 challenges.
.PP
All arguments are named flags. Positional arguments are not accepted;
every subcommand takes \fB\-d\fR / \fB\-\-domain\fR and/or
\fB\-r\fR / \fB\-\-registrar\fR as appropriate.
.PP
Credentials are read from the root\-only SQLite database at
\fB/var/lib/a2tools/creds.db\fR (mode 0600) that \fBfqdncredmgr\fR(1)
manages. No daemon, no socket, no environment variables.
.PP
Available subcommands (use \fB\-\-help\fR for the full list):
.TP
.B check
Print the status of a domain (\fBfree\fR / \fBowned\fR / \fBtaken\fR).
Requires \fB\-d\fR; \fB\-r\fR is optional (hints at the registrar).
.TP
.B purchase
Buy a domain via the configured registrar.
Requires \fB\-d\fR and \fB\-r\fR.
.TP
.B list
List domains associated with a registrar account, or all locally
tracked domains when no \fB\-r\fR is given. With \fB\-r\fR, \fB\-m
local\fR queries the local DB and \fB\-m remote\fR hits the registrar
API.
.TP
.B certify
\fBcertbot\fR manual\-auth hook. Set the ACME TXT challenge record
for the registrar specified by \fB\-r\fR.
.TP
.B cleanup
\fBcertbot\fR manual\-cleanup hook. Remove the ACME TXT challenge
record for the registrar specified by \fB\-r\fR.
.TP
.B setInitDNSRecords
Set the initial DNS records (\fBA\fR, mail MX) for the listed domains.
With \fB\-r\fR only, apply to every domain on the given registrar.
With \fB\-\-sync\fR, block until propagation is confirmed.
.TP
.B checkInitDns
Check whether the initial DNS records for a domain have propagated.
Requires \fB\-d\fR.
.PP
\fBsetInitDNSRecords\fR polls the configured nameservers and Google DNS
\fB8.8.8.8\fR for propagation using exponentially decaying checkpoints
capped at the historical average for that provider, with a 10 second
safety buffer. The check is always run before \fBcertbot\fR is invoked,
to avoid a certbot crash on missing DNS.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-domain " " \fIFQDN\fR
Domain to operate on. For \fBsetInitDNSRecords\fR, may be passed
multiple times (or as a space\-separated list in one \fB\-d\fR value)
to process several domains in a single run.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-registrar " " \fIREGISTRAR\fR
Registrar slug (e.g. \fBnamecheap.com\fR).
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-mode " " { \fBlocal\fR | \fBremote\fR }
List source (only meaningful for \fBlist\fR with \fB\-r\fR).
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-override
\fBsetInitDNSRecords\fR: delete all existing DNS records before
setting the initial ones.
.TP
.BR \-\-sync
\fBsetInitDNSRecords\fR: block until DNS propagation is confirmed.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-timeout " " \fISECONDS\fR
\fBsetInitDNSRecords\fR: maximum time to wait for DNS propagation
(default: 600).
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Print progress on the controlling terminal.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the embedded usage text and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B >0
The registrar API returned an error, propagation timed out, or a
required parameter was missing.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Check the status of a domain:
.RS
.nf
sudo fqdnmgr check -d example.com
sudo fqdnmgr check -d example.com -r namecheap.com -v
.fi
.RE
.PP
Purchase a domain:
.RS
.nf
sudo fqdnmgr purchase -d example.com -r namecheap.com
.fi
.RE
.PP
Set initial DNS records and wait for propagation:
.RS
.nf
sudo fqdnmgr setInitDNSRecords -d example.com --sync -v
sudo fqdnmgr setInitDNSRecords -r namecheap.com --sync
.fi
.RE
.PP
List domains tracked locally, or fetched from a registrar:
.RS
.nf
sudo fqdnmgr list
sudo fqdnmgr list -r namecheap.com -m local
sudo fqdnmgr list -r namecheap.com -m remote
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/a2tools/creds.db
Provider credentials (read by the provider plugins).
.TP
.I /var/cache/a2tools/a2tools.cache
Propagation, whois and NS cache.
.TP
.I /var/log/a2tools/fqdnmgr.log
Request / response log and operational messages.
.TP
.I /etc/a2tools/providers/
Local provider plugin overrides.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/a2tools/providers/
Shipped provider plugins.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR a2sitemgr (1),
.BR a2certrenew (1),
.BR fqdncredmgr (1),
.BR certbot (1)
.PP
